#: ../../source/guides/formats/advanced/semistructured.md:1
msgid "The semistructured level"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/advanced/semistructured.md:3
msgid ""
"Between the two others. The algorithm has a **name**; you say which name "
"serves which segment, and configure it in YAML."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/advanced/semistructured.md:6
msgid "The two files a semistructured format needs"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/advanced/semistructured.md:7
msgid ""
"`content/algorithms/semistructured/formats_mapping.csv` says which named "
"algorithm serves which segment of which pipeline:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/advanced/semistructured.md:15
msgid ""
"An empty cell leaves that segment unspecified at this level, so another "
"level can supply it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/advanced/semistructured.md:17
msgid "One YAML file per segment carries the configuration, under `args/`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/advanced/semistructured.md:31
msgid "The key that links a format to an algorithm"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/advanced/semistructured.md:32
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"`{format}({pipeline})`, falling back to the bare `{format}` only for the "
"**unnamed** pipeline. The two forms are not interchangeable: writing "
"`AMUNDI-IT24` when the pipeline has a name will not be found, and the "
"failure is silent in the sense that the segment simply has no "
"configuration."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/advanced/semistructured.md:36
msgid "Lists, and the counter that indexes them"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/advanced/semistructured.md:38
msgid ""
"Where a value is a **list**, the element used is chosen by **how many "
"pipes have already been emitted for that pipeline and segment** — not by "
"the row's position in the mapping table."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/advanced/semistructured.md:48
msgid ""
"An algorithm that returns three pipes advances that counter by **three**."
" This is the rule that surprises people, and it is worth restating: the "
"counter follows the pipes actually produced, so adding an algorithm "
"earlier in the same segment shifts every list index after it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/advanced/semistructured.md:52
msgid "Algorithm names of your own"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/advanced/semistructured.md:53
msgid ""
"An algorithm name may be implemented natively or by you, in your "
"repository's Python."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/advanced/semistructured.md:55
msgid ""
"Defining the same name **both** ways is an **error**, not a precedence to"
" be remembered. The check runs over every native name of the segment as "
"soon as your module loads."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/advanced/semistructured.md:58
msgid ""
"A collision is nearly always a typo, and letting one side win silently is"
" what makes a typo expensive — you would be debugging an algorithm you "
"did not write while reading the one you did."
msgstr ""

